# Rendered output: ~220 MB, and every byte of it is reproducible from the code
# in this directory (make_figures.py / make_chamber.py / make_anim.py).  Keep it
# out of the repository; the DAQ web page serves report.html straight from disk.
figures/
animations/

# Sampled opening-angle shapes for the X17 figure. Regenerates itself from
# MX17_Simulation on first render (~1 min); cached only to keep re-renders fast.
.cache/

# The printed deck: ~38 MB, and `slides/make_pdf.sh` rebuilds it from
# index.html in about a minute.  index.html IS the deck and is tracked; this is
# a backup for the conference laptop, not a source.
slides/mpgd26_talk_draft.pdf

# NOTE on the slide images: the repository's top-level .gitignore ignores *.png,
# so slides/assets/img/*.png is NOT tracked -- every one of them is a render and
# NOTES.md carries the command that makes it.  The .jpg files there ARE tracked,
# because photographs cannot be regenerated.  Full-resolution originals of ours
# live in photos/; see make_photos.py.

# ...and the same rule for the vector copies a few figures write beside their
# PNG (make_timeline.py does): a render, regenerated by one command.
slides/assets/img/*.pdf

# The PowerPoint translation of the deck: ~49 MB, and `slides/to_pptx.py`
# rebuilds it from index.html in about two minutes.  Since 2026-08-26 the .pptx
# is the deck of RECORD and index.html is frozen, so a re-export is a
# start-over rather than a sync -- see slides/NOTES.md.
#
# The glob also catches the dated backups taken before a hand edit
# (mpgd26_talk_<date>_<what>.pptx), and the .pdf line the printed copy: same
# bulk, and neither is a source.
slides/mpgd26_talk*.pptx
slides/mpgd26_talk*.pdf
slides/_pptx_measure.json
slides/_measure.html
slides/svg/
